  "worked_solution": "Let $p$ represent the profit on a single roll of the game. On each roll in the game, there are two possible outcomes:\n\n- If rolling gives an odd number ($1$, $3,$ or $5$), the player loses $$4,$ so we have $p=-4.$\n\n- If rolling gives an even number ($2$, $4,$ or $6$), the player wins $$11,$ so we have $p=11.$\n\nThe probabilities for the outcomes are\n\n$$\nP(-4)=\\frac{2}{3},\\,P(11)=\\frac{1}{3}.\n$$\n\nLet's summarize this in a table.  If $p$ is the profit (in dollars) on a single game, and $f(p)$ is the probability mass function for $p,$ then we have the following:\n\n| $f(p)$ | $\\frac{2}{3}$ | $\\frac{1}{3}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $p$ | $-4$ | $11$ |\n\nTherefore, the expected value of $p$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}E[p] & =(-4)\\cdot f(-4)+11\\cdot f(11) \\\\  & =(-4)(\\frac{2}{3})+11(\\frac{1}{3}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{8}{3}+\\frac{11}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{-8+11}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{3} \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the expected profit is $$1.00.$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
